  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (rna_only, multiprofile, pca_n2000, avgpool) achieves 0.591 acc, substantially better than singleprofile (0.485), confirming multiprofile + aggregation is the strongest direction so far. However, we have no evidence about whether the aggregation method itself matters—avgpool is the simplest option. Question: config_003 is identical to config_002 except it replaces avgpool with a transformer aggregator, giving a clean single-variable test of whether learned attention-based profile combination captures interactions that simple averaging misses. Why this is the best next experiment: it directly extends our strongest result with a minimal, interpretable change; the outcome (transformer >> avgpool, ≈, or <<) will determine the aggregation architecture for all subsequent multimodal experiments, making it high-information per budget unit. It also avoids the risk of confounding encoder choice (scvi/scgpt) with aggregation choice in a single step."
